Package: da4linux
Version: 0.1.0-1
Architecture: all
Maintainer: DA4Linux Project <da4linux@proton.me>
Installed-Size: 643
Depends: pipewire (>= 1.0)
Recommends: wireplumber, lsp-plugins-lv2, calf-plugins
Suggests: libmysofa-utils
Section: sound
Priority: optional
Homepage: https://github.com/menak02/DA4Linux
Description: Dolby Audio-like processing for Linux via PipeWire filter-chain
 DA4Linux generates PipeWire filter-chain configurations to enhance
 laptop speaker audio quality using the same DSP techniques found
 in vendor-supplied audio drivers.
 .
 It reads Dolby DAX3 XML tuning files from Windows drivers and produces
 PipeWire-native processing chains with: FIR speaker correction,
 parametric EQ, multiband compression, stereo enhancement, bass
 enhancement, dialogue enhancement, loudness compensation, virtual
 surround, and speaker protection limiting.
 .
 No persistent daemon required — processing runs inside PipeWire.
 Works on any Linux desktop with PipeWire >= 1.0.
